<p>
I don&rsquo;t use social media. Why would I? Who wants some algorithm telling you what to read and filtering your own content? What I <i>do</i> like is RSS. You see messages about <i>all</i> the content from all the sites you&rsquo;re interested in. As I&rsquo;ve said before [<a href="https://irreal.org/blog/?p=12024">1</a>, <a href="https://irreal.org/blog/?p=13323">2</a>], I <i>really</i> like RSS and I&rsquo;m sad that Google and others pushing social media did everything they could to kill it. But, after all, it wasn&rsquo;t monetizable.
</p>
<p>
Fortunately, despite what the pundits will tell you, RSS has survived and is prospering among those who haven&rsquo;t been lobotomized by social media. Among those people is Andrew Shell who has a <a href="https://andrewshell.org/2026/07/i-%e2%99%a5-rss/">site where people who feel similary can list their webpage and agreement</a>.
</p>
<p>
If you have a Web site and agree, send your site&rsquo;s URL to Shell and get your site on his list of sites that love RSS.</p>
